COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from U04045.1, AK304496.1 and
            CB250419.1.
            
            On Aug 31, 2019 this sequence version replaced NM_000251.2.
            
            Summary: This locus is frequently mutated in hereditary
            nonpolyposis colon cancer (HNPCC). When cloned, it was discovered
            to be a human homolog of the E. coli mismatch repair gene mutS,
            consistent with the characteristic alterations in microsatellite
            sequences (RER+ phenotype) found in HNPCC. Two transcript variants
            encoding different isoforms have been found for this gene.
            [provided by RefSeq, Apr 2012].
            
            Transcript Variant: This variant (1) represents the longer
            transcript and encodes the longer isoform (1).
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
